{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in with nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started this afternoon. I ate a little jello after my clinic visit and suddenly had that familiar pain—just like my last flare-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You were discharged just three days ago, correct? And you were feeling okay until today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. I felt great after the last hospitalization. I thought I was past this, but it came on fast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show your potassium is low—3.0—which can happen with vomiting. We’ve already given you some replacement, and we’re starting IV fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I haven’t been able to keep anything down. Is this another gastroparesis flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, everything points to that. Your lipase, liver tests, and lactate are normal, so it’s not pancreatitis or infection. This looks like your usual pattern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank goodness. I was worried it was something new. What about the IV meds I usually get?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you IV ondansetron, lorazepam, and prochlorperazine—just like before. Morphine too, if you need it for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Those usually help a lot. Can I try to eat anything tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-04-05 17:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We’ll keep you on bowel rest tonight and start with small sips tomorrow if you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-04-06 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your potassium is back to normal, and you haven’t vomited since last night. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-04-06 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. The pain is gone, and I feel like I could try some food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-04-06 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll start you on clear liquids and see how you do. If that goes well, you can advance to solids later today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve tolerated the liquids well. We’re going to discharge you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. Should I keep using my J-tube at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the nutrition team recommends using it to rest your stomach. Home health will help set that up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what about the nausea meds? I’d like something to take at home when this happens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you a prescription for ondansetron—Zofran—5 tablets to start. Your insurance doesn’t cover it, so you’ll need to pay out of pocket to try it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it. I already have Ativan and Tigan at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. We’re not prescribing oral morphine because it can worsen gastroparesis. But Zofran might help catch it early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Should I follow up with Dr. ___?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please schedule an appointment with your GI specialist to discuss long-term management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my thyroid meds? I’m still taking levothyroxine at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue that as usual. Your thyroid levels are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much more like myself now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Home health will contact you about the J-tube support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-04-06 10:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll follow all the instructions. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-04-05 17:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-04-06 15:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of gastroparesis, J-tube placement, and Nissen fundoplication was admitted for recurrent nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain, consistent with her prior flares. She had been discharged three days earlier but developed symptoms suddenly after eating a small amount of jello. In the ED, she was found to have hypokalemia, which was corrected with IV potassium. She was treated with IV fluids, bowel rest, and IV antiemetics including ondansetron, lorazepam, and prochlorperazine, with good symptom control. Her pain resolved overnight, and she advanced to oral intake. Labs remained stable, with no signs of infection or organ dysfunction. She was discharged home with instructions to use her J-tube for feeds, try oral ondansetron (Zofran) for breakthrough nausea, and follow up with her gastroenterologist. Home health services were arranged for J-tube support.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Dehydration",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Status of other artificial opening of gastrointestinal tract",
      "Dyskinesia of esophagus",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
